{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"b957a930-8828-4833-abd0-2d7504378af2","status":"SUCCESS","response":"### 1. `01_intake`\n- **Scope**: Repair [schema.py](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/tmp/disposable_workspaces/live_BENCH-011_26428_1795226112894_icm/schema.py), [upcaster.py](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/tmp/disposable_workspaces/live_BENCH-011_26428_1795226112894_icm/upcaster.py), [store.py](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/tmp/disposable_workspaces/live_BENCH-011_26428_1795226112894_icm/store.py), and [projector.py](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/tmp/disposable_workspaces/live_BENCH-011_26428_1795226112894_icm/projector.py) using Python stdlib only.\n- **Constraints**: Preserve public API, enforce strict type/value validation, deep-copy isolation, optimistic concurrency, chained upcasting, and snapshot-plus-tail replay.\n\n### 2. `02_plan`\n- **Impacted files \u0026 acceptance criteria**:\n  - [schema.py](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/tmp/disposable_workspaces/live_BENCH-011_26428_1795226112894_icm/schema.py): Validate `Event.schema_version` is `int` (not `bool`) in `{1, 2, 3}`.\n  - [upcaster.py](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/tmp/disposable_workspaces/live_BENCH-011_26428_1795226112894_icm/upcaster.py): Chain `v1 -\u003e v2 -\u003e v3` sequentially and raise `ValueError` if `v1` lacks `\"amount\"`.\n  - [store.py](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/tmp/disposable_workspaces/live_BENCH-011_26428_1795226112894_icm/store.py): Check `expected_version != current` (raising `ConflictError`), deep-copy events on `append` (returning independent copies without mutating caller inputs), and return deep copies from `read`.\n  - [projector.py](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/tmp/disposable_workspaces/live_BENCH-011_26428_1795226112894_icm/projector.py): Pass `after_version=version` to `store.read` in `replay`.\n\n### 3. `03_exec`\n- Applied targeted edits to:\n  - `Event.__post_init__` in [schema.py](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/tmp/disposable_workspaces/live_BENCH-011_26428_1795226112894_icm/schema.py#L19-L20)\n  - `upcast` in [upcaster.py](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/tmp/disposable_workspaces/live_BENCH-011_26428_1795226112894_icm/upcaster.py#L9-L17)\n  - `EventStore.append` and `EventStore.read` in [store.py](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/tmp/disposable_workspaces/live_BENCH-011_26428_1795226112894_icm/store.py#L16-L34)\n  - `replay` in [projector.py](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/tmp/disposable_workspaces/live_BENCH-011_26428_1795226112894_icm/projector.py#L19)\n\n### 4. `04_verify`\n- `python -m pytest -q`: `1 passed in 0.02s`.\n- Inline invariant verification (`schema_version` validation, `v1 -\u003e v3` chained upcasting, `ConflictError` on mismatched `expected_version` including empty appends, deep-copy isolation on `append`/`read`, and `replay` with/without snapshots): `ALL_CHECKS_PASSED`.\n\n### 5. `05_retro`\n- All four bugs stemmed from missing boundary/isolation checks (`schema_version` validation, `elif` breaking `v1 -\u003e v3` chaining, `expected_version \u003e current` + shared references in `EventStore`, and `after_version=0` in `replay`). No follow-up edits needed.\n","duration_seconds":42.66381,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":37223,"output_tokens":4852,"thinking_tokens":1550,"cache_read_tokens":104842,"total_tokens":42075}}}
